Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:01:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/24] Check the raw log and journal before a log shrink; gate
 slot clearing

From the review of the log-shrink gate: EmptyLog checked only the WAL's
logical length, so a conversion's legacy header backup and journal
(after the drain emptied the WAL) relied on an explicit check alone; it
now counts the raw log and an outstanding journal, and ShrinkLog counts
a journal retired without a length change. Clearing retired WAL slots
goes through the same check. A unit test calls ShrinkLog on an engine
that has not synced the data file and after an uncovered data write.
Comment and doc fixes; the shared proof test asserts the dispose path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
